    {
      "path": "django/db/models/query.py",
      "lines": [
        81,
        88
      ],
      "comment": "__aiter__() is a *synchronous* method that has to then return an *asynchronous* iterator/generator. Thus, nest an async generator inside it. This is a generic iterable converter for now, and is going to suffer a performance penalty on large sets of items due to the cost of crossing over the sync barrier for each chunk. Custom __aiter__() methods should be added to each Iterable subclass, but that needs some work in the Compiler first.",
